<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Baobab sees improved earnings at year end.</title>
<headline>Baobab sees improved earnings at year end.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December</p>
<p>31, 1996.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Retained income at</p>
<p>    beginning of period    8.47	   vs 7.94</p>
<p>Retained income at</p>
<p>    end of period	    9.29	   vs 7.95</p>
<p>    Interest received	1.02	   vs 0.66</p>
<p>    Dividends received     0.69	   vs  -</p>
<p>    Administration costs   0.82 (loss)  vs 0.66 (loss)</p>
<p>Full name: Baobab Solid Growth Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it expected attributable earnings for the year to June 30, 1997 to be at least 19.6 million rand. These would come from existing investments Premier Freight, King Finance and Mercantile Lisbon Bank Holdings, as well as from new investments in ATIO Corporation and Altfin.</p>
<p>Shares in holding company Mustek would be listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange on April 3, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
